13:["$","section",null,{"id":"editing","className":"paper-section","aria-labelledby":"editing-title","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"section-intro","children":[["$","h2",null,{"id":"editing-title","children":"What happens when a part changes?"}],["$","p",null,{"children":["A ",["$","strong",null,{"children":"parent"}]," is the part another part attaches to; the attached part is its ",["$","strong",null,{"children":"child"}],". For example, a bird’s feet (child) attach to its body (parent). Default renders tell only part of the story. The paper compares what happens after the parent shrinks or the child grows, testing whether the intended connections remain intact."]}]]}],["$","$L15",null,{}]]}]
